    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The change is complete and the test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe requirement was to return `selfLink` = `/api/owners/` + the new owner id on the owner resource. The `OwnerDto` is generated at build time from the OpenAPI spec, and derived fields are populated by MapStruct in `OwnerMapper`, so I made two changes following the existing conventions:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `selfLink` string property to the `Owner` schema (alongside `id`, `displayName`, etc.), so the generated `OwnerDto` gains a `selfLink` field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added `@Mapping(target = \"selfLink\", expression = \"java(selfLink(owner))\")` to `toOwnerDto`, plus a `selfLink(Owner)` helper that returns `\"/api/owners/\" + owner.getId()` (null when the owner has no id), mirroring the other derived-field helpers.\n\n`GET /api/owners/{id}` now includes `\"selfLink\": \"/api/owners/{id}\"`. The full test suite passes (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`, BUILD SUCCESS), including the new `AcceptanceTest.coreReturnsSelfLink`.",
